WHAT THIS IS. Issue #41 (SF-2, epic #39) mirrors a cmux run into the #40 ledger. be-41-01 shipped scripts/factory/emit.mjs (the never-throwing facade + run sidecar), be-41-02 shipped scripts/factory/transcript.mjs (the reducer + resolver), be-41-03 made claude_session_id === record.dispatch_id by passing --session-id from buildArgv. This slice is the call-site wiring for five verbs; be-41-05 does closeCmd in the same file, serialized after this one. Design of record: .claude/dev-team/tasks/issue-41/architecture-package-v1.md (sections 5.4, 5.5, 5.6).

EMISSION MAP — exactly these sites, all additive:
  workspaceCmd (dispatch.mjs:803)  -> create or adopt the sidecar; emitter.startRun() = startSession{adw_id, repo_slug, task_slug} + startPhase{name:'planning'}
  dispatchCmd (:1299)              -> emitter.phaseTransition('building') (idempotent: endPhase(prev)+startPhase); recordEvent{agent_start,{role,model,dispatch_id}}; sidecar dispatches[dispatch_id] = {claude_session_id: record.dispatch_id, transcript_path: null, session_started: false, sighted_at: null}
  phaseCmd (:2615)                 -> on --set gate: emitter.phaseTransition('gate')
  awaitCmd (:1825)                 -> per tick: resolveTranscript for each unresolved dispatch -> first sighting pins the path and calls startAgentSession; then heartbeat{target:'agent_session'} throttled >= 15s per session; relaySignals(...).recorded -> mapSignalLogEntries -> recordEvent{log,...}; installFinalizer (this verb ONLY)
  teardownCmd (:2510)              -> reconcile open agent sessions from the sidecar; endPhase(open) + endSession{status, billed_* from the sidecar accumulator}; the stats snapshot event
  statusCmd (:2349)                -> NOTHING (read verb stays emission-free)

WHERE TO HOOK IN awaitCmd — the poll loop already exists; you are adding to it, not restructuring it. dispatch.mjs:1927-1941 and the tick bound at :2015:
      const resolvedNow = []
      const currentAttentionIds = new Set()
      for (const id of [...remaining]) {
        const record = findRecordByDispatchId(paths.dispatchDir, id)
        if (!record) { remaining.delete(id); continue }
        const sidecars = sidecarPaths(paths, id)
        const fsState = collectFsState({ record, paths: { exitPath: sidecars.exit, gatePath: sidecars.gate } })
        const classification = classify({ record, fsState, tree: null, now: now(), turnEndAt: turnEndAt[id] ?? null })
        ...
      }
      ...
      sleep(Math.min(tickMs, Math.max(capS * 1000 - elapsedMs, 0)))
Per-dispatch resolution goes inside that for-loop; the heartbeat pass and the signals pass go after it, before the sleep. The loop's deps are already injectable — dispatch.mjs:1822-1829: 'awaitCmd(args, ctx, deps) -> { code, json }. deps = { now, sleep, tickMs } are overridable so tests never sleep real wall-clock time'; tickMs defaults to AWAIT_TICK_MS_DEFAULT = 4000 (:1788). awaitCmd's two return shapes are at :1987-1998 (resolved/remaining/attention) and :2005-2012 (status:'still-running'); its lock-held early return is at :1856 ({code:2, json:{error:'lock_held', holder}}). All three must stay byte-identical.

VERB RETURN SHAPES TO FREEZE (this is the deepEqual list): preflight :773 · workspace (json built near the end of workspaceCmd) · dispatch (dispatchCmd's return) · await :1987-1998 / :2005-2012 / :1856 · close :2334-2342 (be-41-05 owns it) · status :2463-2465 · teardown :2580 {task_dir, state_dir, leftover_worktrees} · phase :2638 {phase: args.set}. main() prints result.json and returns result.code (:2841-2904) — an added key would change every consumer's parse, which is exactly what the frozen deepEqual catches.

LEDGER SIGNATURES YOU CALL THROUGH THE FACADE (scripts/factory/ledger.mjs; do NOT edit that file — ADR-026): startSession({adw_id, repo_slug, task_slug}) :669 · endSession({adw_id, status, billed_*}) :694 · startPhase({adw_id, name, seq}) -> phaseId | null :734 · endPhase({adw_id, seq, status}) :768 · recordEvent({adw_id, type, seq, phase_id, payload, started_at?, ended_at?}) :785 · heartbeat({adw_id, target:'agent_session', claude_session_id, at}) :934 · startAgentSession({adw_id, dispatch_id, role, model, claude_session_id, transcript_path, started_at}) :963 · endAgentSession({adw_id, claude_session_id, + eight token fields}) :993. startPhase returns null in degraded mode, so phase_id is passed as explicit NULL downstream, never omitted (requireFields rejects only undefined, :645-655). recordEvent REFUSES type 'heartbeat' (:787-792) — use the heartbeat writer.

WHY THE ORDERING MATTERS (verified, and the reason be-41-03 exists): heartbeat's agent_session branch is UPDATE agent_sessions SET last_heartbeat_at = ? WHERE adw_id = ? AND claude_session_id = ? (ledger.mjs:956), and startAgentSession is the ONLY writer of transcript_path (:963-991 — endAgentSession does not update it, :993-1028). So a session whose transcript is never sighted lands transcript_path as explicit null and can never be back-filled inside #41 (OD-11, a ledger.mjs change, out of scope); the provenance for that case lives in the sidecar.

ABNORMAL EXIT (section 5.6, and the one deliberate behaviour delta): installFinalizer is opt-in and never installed at import (ledger.mjs:1174, :1202; impl :1274-1317). Install it in awaitCmd ONLY — that is the single verb with a long-lived process and an open session (up to AWAIT_CAP_MAX_S = 600s, dispatch.mjs:1791) and the realistic SIGINT target. On SIGTERM/SIGINT it lands endSession{status:'fail'} from the IN-PROCESS registry (never the mirror), ends running processes as killed, sets process.exitCode = 128 + signum and re-raises (:1314-1317). It therefore DOES change awaitCmd's exit code on a signal — pre-existing ledger.mjs behaviour on a path that was already terminating abnormally. Assert it (an interrupted await still exits 130 on SIGINT, not 0) so a reviewer does not read it as the constraint violation. Stale open agent_sessions rows are teardown's job because installFinalizerImpl reconciles sessions and processes, NOT agent sessions (:1274-1313); a run that never reaches teardown keeps its stale row — an accepted, stated limitation.

SIGNALS — READ THIS BEFORE WIRING IT. relaySignals lives in scripts/cmux/ladder.mjs and is currently PRODUCTION-UNWIRED (called only from test/cmux-ladder.test.mjs). Its `recorded` array is NOT the validated stream: :711-717 pushes schema-INVALID parsed objects into `recorded` AND into `dropped`, then continues; only malformed JSON is excluded (:707). The SIGNAL_LEVELS clamp (:719) and the SIGNAL_LIMITS.message_max_chars cap (:741) are applied on the RELAY path only. Two traps: consuming `recorded` as if validated, and performing the unbuilt relay side effect. SIGNAL_LIMITS is exported from scripts/cmux/contract.mjs:41 and dispatch.mjs already imports from './contract.mjs' (line 62) — add SIGNAL_LIMITS to that import list. SIGNAL_LEVELS is module-private in ladder.mjs, derived from signal-record.schema.json's own `level` enum (ladder.mjs:18-19) — derive it the SAME way in dispatch.mjs (read the same schema.json file), rather than importing a private constant or editing ladder.mjs. Pass both into emitter.mapSignalLogEntries so there is still exactly one source of truth (the schema file), never a second hand-written enum.

TEST PLUMBING THAT ALREADY EXISTS: test/cmux-dispatch.test.mjs's buildTestCtx + the fake-cmux fixture (test/fixtures/fake-cmux.mjs — logs every invocation as one JSON line to $FAKE_CMUX_LOG, persists topology to $FAKE_CMUX_STATE, varies only by env switches). Count notify invocations from that log for the zero-relay assertion. Known trap (backend-notes.md 2026-08-08): buildTestCtx silently ignores its opts.root parameter — do not build a new assertion on that parameter without checking it takes effect.

ASSUMPTIONS STATED SO YOU CAN FLAG THEM: (1) one adw_id per (repo, task) run, minted at workspace time and retired at teardown (user decision D1) — that is why parallel dispatch verbs contend for one seq space. (2) 'live pids'/processes rows are descoped to 'live liveness' (user decision D2) — do NOT call startProcess/endProcess; ledger kill stays unusable for panes. (3) A missing gate phase (the orchestrator never running phase --set gate) yields a SPARSE trail, never a wrong one — never infer a phase from activity, that would originate a fact. (4) The mirror covers cmux-mode runs only; an agent-tool run produces zero rows (ADR-026 clause 6) — do not add a producer anywhere else.
